PHASE 3H — PREDICTION CALIBRATION LAYER

OBJECTIVE:
Fix the empirically demonstrated cross-position xP calibration problems
identified in Phase 3G.

DO NOT modify the optimizer yet.

DO NOT manually boost Haaland, Bruno, Saka, or any other player.

DO NOT use ownership or FPL consensus as a prediction target.

DO NOT hard-code positional bonuses.

The goal is to make the predicted FPL point distribution empirically
match historical FPL outcomes.

==================================================
BACKGROUND — PHASE 3G FINDINGS
==================================================

Phase 3G evaluated 62,437 leak-free historical player-GW observations.

The current production xP scale was found to be systematically
miscalibrated.

Key findings:

1. £4.5m–£7.0m defenders projected at 4.5–6.0 xP:

Predicted mean: 4.84
Actual mean:    2.74

Bias: -2.10 points/match

2. £10m+ premium attackers projected at 4.0–5.5 xP:

Predicted mean: 4.66
Actual mean:    6.03

Bias: +1.37 points/match

3. Premium attackers overall:

Predicted xP: 2.98
Actual FPL points: 5.05

Underprediction: +2.07 points/match

4. Clean sheets:

Predicted probability: 34.5%
Actual rate:            13.3%

5. £10m+ attacker xG:

Predicted: 0.253
Actual goals: 0.435

6. £10m+ attacker xA:

Predicted: 0.087
Actual assists: 0.253

7. Current xP is therefore NOT safe to feed directly into the optimizer.

The Phase 3G report is the ground truth for this phase.

==================================================
CORE PRINCIPLE
==================================================

We are NOT going to solve this by saying:

"Haaland should score more because everyone knows Haaland is good."

Instead:

Historical predictions → actual historical outcomes

must be used to learn a calibration transformation.

The desired pipeline is:

Underlying football models
        ↓
Raw xG / xA / CS / DEFCON / Minutes
        ↓
FPL scoring engine
        ↓
RAW xP
        ↓
CALIBRATION LAYER
        ↓
CALIBRATED xP
        ↓
optimizer

The calibration layer must be learned from historical data and
validated out-of-sample.

